# Supabase — copy to .env and fill in from your project's
# Settings > API page. Both values are safe to ship in a desktop client:
# the anon key is publishable by design and every table is protected by RLS.
#
# Keep the real values in .env, which is gitignored. This file is committed,
# so leaving values here puts your project ref in git history for good and
# hands anyone who clones the repo your project instead of a blank template.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key in either file. It bypasses RLS entirely.
# It belongs only on the payments website's server, never in a desktop app.
#
# The MAIN_VITE_ prefix is required. electron-vite only inlines variables
# with that prefix into the main-process bundle, which is what makes them
# readable via import.meta.env in a PACKAGED app — a plain process.env read
# works under `npm run dev` and then comes back undefined once built.
MAIN_VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
MAIN_VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional. Where Settings > Account > Cloud Sync sends people once the
# payments website exists. Unset, that section renders as "Coming soon"
# with the button disabled rather than opening a dead link.
RENDERER_VITE_UPGRADE_URL=
